{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Is your elderly father, of whom you spoke, well — is he still alive?</b> He was asking about Yitzhak his grandfather, and they answered him about Ya'akov: ״לעבדך לאבינו עודנו חי״. But Yitzhak is not alive, and they did not want to answer him plainly that Yitzhak had died, for one does not respond to a breach — as we find at the beginning of פסחים: ״אייבו קיים״ — ״אימא קיימת״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:00.692827438Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}